  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "`new_object` incorrectly lets a DXF group-code 310 binary pair fall through to the generic common-field setter for the malloc-owned entity `preview` field when the specialized preview path is not applicable (notably when the subclass is not `AcDbEntity`). `dwg_dynapi_common_set_value(..., &pair->value, 1)` then shallow-copies the `pair->value.s` pointer into `obj->tio.entity->preview`; `new_object` subsequently calls `dxf_free_pair`, which frees that same buffer without clearing the entity alias. On error cleanup, `dwg_free_common_entity_data` frees the dangling `preview` pointer again at `free.c:414`, causing the observed double-free. The root is the unsafe generic handling/ownership transfer in `new_object`, rather than the final free routine.",
    "conditions": "A text DXF must create an entity (the PoV uses `DIMENSION`, ultimately `DIMENSION_ANG2LN`) and supply a code-310 binary/string value while parser subclass state does not satisfy the dedicated `add_ent_preview` condition (`subclass == \"AcDbEntity\"`). The malformed 1002/360/310 sequence in the PoV causes code 310 to match the common `preview` metadata and take the generic setter path. The pair's allocated value is shallow-stored as `entity->preview` and then freed by normal pair cleanup. A subsequent parse failure/critical return (as in the PoV's further malformed 360/310 data) invokes `dwg_free`, which frees the stale preview pointer a second time. Any later teardown of such an entity can trigger the same ownership error once this generic 310 path has been taken."
  },
